<title>INDIA: INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, SOYOIL UP IN THIN TRADE.</title>
<headline>INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, SOYOIL UP IN THIN TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices ended steady in light trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said soybean sowing was in progress in several areas of central India.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne in thin trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $262-263 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports against Monday's $264-265.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $94 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
